  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gender equality</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">DFAT provided $14.6million to women&#x2019;s rights organisations in the Indo Pacific since 2021, through partnerships with four Women&#x2019;s Funds: Women&#x2019;s Fund Asia, Urgent Action Fund Asia &amp; Pacific, Women&#x2019;s Fund Fiji and the Pacific Feminist Fund. Together, in 2024, these Women&#x2019;s Funds disbursed 156 grants across 25 countries in the Indo Pacific. A 2025 evaluation of the AIR pilot partnership found that working with Women&#x2019;s Funds is a highly effective way to support locally led approaches to gender equality, disability equity and social inclusion and to reach the most marginalized women.
&#x200d;
A key achievement of the AIR pilot was the incubation of the Pacific Feminist Fund &#x2013; the first Pacific regional Women&#x2019;s Fund &#x2013; through support by the AIR Women&#x2019;s Fund partners. The AIR pilot also enabled the Women&#x2019;s Funds to improve language accessibility and access to grants for women with disability and their organisations, and use their extensive networks to identify and reach groups otherwise excluded from traditional donor funding, including small and emerging local organisations. Grants provided through the AIR pilot have enabled these groups to drive community-led changes to advance gender equality.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gender equality</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under the Amplify-Invest-Reach (A-I-R) Partnership, DFAT provided funding to Women&#x2019;s Rights Organisations. Through A-I-R, with Australian Funding, key partners Women&#x2019;s Fund Asia, Urgent Action Fund for Women&#x2019;s Human Rights &#x2013; Asia &amp; Pacific, Women&#x2019;s Fund Fiji and the Pacific Feminist Fund made grants to 79 women&#x2019;s rights organisations in 25 countries in Asia and the Pacific. A-I-R is a catalytic investment in the critical work of women&#x2019;s funds to support human rights defenders and advocacy for the rights of women, girls and other groups experiencing marginalisation in countries across the Indo-Pacific region.</narrative>
    </description>
